1
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:28,500
The end is near.

2
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Chicken Little is a animation, family, comedy film directed by Mark Dindal.

3
00:10:07,500 --> 00:10:13,500
When the sky really is falling and sanity has flown the
coop, who will rise to save the day?

4
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:36,000
Together with his hysterical band of misfit friends, Chicken Little must hatch a plan to save the
planet from alien invasion and prove that the world's biggest hero is a little chicken.

5
00:16:52,500 --> 00:16:58,500
Chicken Little (voice), played by Zach Braff.

6
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:21,000
Buck Cluck (voice), played by Garry Marshall.

7
00:23:37,500 --> 00:23:43,500
Mayor Turkey Lurkey (voice), played by Don Knotts.

8
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:06,000
Foxy Loxy (voice), played by Amy Sedaris.

9
00:30:22,500 --> 00:30:28,500
Runt of the Litter (voice), played by Steve Zahn.

10
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:51,000
Abby Mallard (voice), played by Joan Cusack.

11
00:37:07,500 --> 00:37:13,500
Chicken Little is a 2005 American animated science fiction comedy
film produced by Walt Disney Feature Animation.

12
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:36,000
It is loosely inspired by the European folk tale "Henny Penny",
known in the United States as "Chicken Little".

13
00:43:52,500 --> 00:43:58,500
Disney had previously adapted the tale in a 1943 short film.

14
00:47:15,000 --> 00:47:21,000
The film follows Chicken Little who, after claiming the sky was "falling" and subsequently being ridiculed
by his town, attempts to fix his reputation, only to discover an otherworldly revelation.

15
00:50:37,500 --> 00:50:43,500
The film was directed by Mark Dindal and written by Steve Bencich, Ron J.

16
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Friedman, and Ron Anderson, and features Zach Braff as Chicken Little, with Joan Cusack, Dan Molina,
Steve Zahn, Garry Marshall, Amy Sedaris, Mark Walton, and Don Knotts in supporting roles.

17
00:57:22,500 --> 00:57:28,500
Chicken Little was animated in-house at Walt Disney Feature
Animation's main headquarters in Burbank, California.

18
01:00:45,000 --> 01:00:51,000
It was Disney Animation's first fully computer-animated feature film.

19
01:04:07,500 --> 01:04:13,500
Chicken Little premiered at the El Capitan Theatre in Hollywood on October 30, 2005, and
was released in the United States on November 4, by Walt Disney Pictures.

20
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
It was the first mainstream theatrical release in Digital 3-D, with around 100
theaters worldwide fitted with new 3-D projectors to screen the film.

21
01:10:52,500 --> 01:10:58,500
It received mixed reviews from critics and grossed $314 million,
becoming the second-highest-grossing animated film of 2005.

22
01:14:15,000 --> 01:14:21,000
The film explores themes of fish, small town, space marine, superhero, chicken.

23
01:17:37,500 --> 01:17:43,500
The tone is lighthearted.
